  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run, with all 18 witnesses passing, so I used 1 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_450_1m.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`) whose footprint overlaps a bridge, viaduct or tunnel (any `elevated_structure` region).\n- **The duty:** the vehicle must not be at rest, meaning its speed must stay above `p.halt_speed_tolerance`, unless one of two exceptions holds:\n  - **Traffic ahead:** another member of traffic is ahead of it in the same lane, with the gap between their bodies at most `p.queue_halt_gap`.\n  - **A command to stop:** a travel region the vehicle occupies is governed by one of these:\n    - a stop sign or a yield sign;\n    - a traffic signal showing circular red, a red arrow (any direction) or flashing red;\n    - a level-crossing signal with its lights flashing, or its gate lowering or down;\n    - a police officer directing it to stop.\n- **Two choices, both within the blueprint's wording,** so I declared no narrowings:\n  - The blueprint's \"in compliance with law\" exception (stop sign and red signal) is fully contained in its traffic-control-device exception. I wrote the combined list once, because repeating the stop sign and red signal would create duplicate checks that no test scene could tell apart.\n  - The exceptions are part of the duty rather than the conditions for applying it. So a halt behind traffic counts as compliant, not \"not applicable\", which matches the planned `branch_1` verdict.\n\n**Test scenes** (`TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_450_1m.lean`): the 6 planned ones, plus 12 more so every exception is tested both ways. Examples:\n- a vehicle ahead 12 m away (violated);\n- a stop sign on the other lane only (violated);\n- a green signal (violated);\n- dark crossing lights with the gate up (violated);\n- a police officer signalling \"proceed\" (violated);\n- a flagger signalling \"stop\" (violated);\n- each matching exception that holds (compliant).\n\nBefore the first gate run, I mistakenly sent one extra shell command: the gate command with `--help` and a pipe added. The permission layer blocked it, so it never ran and didn't count against the budget.\n\nThe full report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
